<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>What is an ARG?</title>
    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        body {
            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;
            background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
            min-height: 100vh;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .container {
            background: white;
            border-radius: 12px;
            box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
            max-width: 700px;
            padding: 40px;
            line-height: 1.8;
        }

        h1 {
            color: #667eea;
            margin-bottom: 25px;
            font-size: 2.5em;
            text-align: center;
        }

        h2 {
            color: #764ba2;
            margin-top: 30px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            font-size: 1.4em;
        }

        p {
            color: #333;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
            font-size: 1.05em;
        }

        .content {
            user-select: none;
            -webkit-user-select: none;
            -moz-user-select: none;
            -ms-user-select: none;
        }

        .hidden-message {
            display: none;
            color: #ff4757;
            font-weight: bold;
            font-size: 1.2em;
            text-align: center;
            margin-top: 20px;
            animation: fadeIn 0.5s ease-in;
        }

        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from { opacity: 0; }
            to { opacity: 1; }
        }

        ul {
            margin-left: 25px;
            margin-bottom: 15px;
        }

        li {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
            color: #444;
        }

        .highlight {
            background-color: #fff3cd;
            padding: 15px;
            border-left: 4px solid #ffc107;
            margin: 20px 0;
            border-radius: 4px;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>What is an ARG?</h1>
        
        <div class="content" id="mainContent">
            <p>An <strong>ARG (Alternate Reality Game)</strong> is an interactive narrative that blurs the line between fiction and reality. Players are immersed in a story that unfolds across multiple platforms and media, often without being told explicitly that it's a game.</p>

            <h2>Key Characteristics</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Immersive Storytelling:</strong> The story feels real and is presented as if it's actually happening</li>
                <li><strong>Multi-platform:</strong> Clues and story elements appear across websites, social media, emails, phone calls, and more</li>
                <li><strong>Community-driven:</strong> Players work together to solve puzzles, decode messages, and uncover the narrative</li>
                <li><strong>Real-time progression:</strong> The story evolves over time, sometimes over weeks or months</li>
                <li><strong>Interactivity:</strong> Players can influence the story through their actions and discoveries</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <p>ARG creators plant cryptic clues, hidden messages, and puzzles for players to discover. These might be:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Encoded text or images</li>
                <li>Hidden websites or Easter eggs</li>
                <li>Mysterious phone calls or emails</li>
                <li>Steganography or cipher puzzles</li>
                <li>Coordinate-based clues pointing to real-world locations</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="highlight">
                <p><strong>Famous ARGs:</strong> The Beast (2001), Lonelygirl15 (2006), Marble Hornets (2009), and Take This Lollipop (2011) are considered landmark ARGs that defined the genre.</p>
            </div>

            <h2>Why People Love ARGs</h2>
            <p>ARGs offer a unique blend of mystery, community, and adventure. They reward curiosity, critical thinking, and collaboration. Players feel like they're part of something bigger than themselves—uncovering a true mystery.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden-message" id="hiddenMsg">
            solve it yourself. I am not an ARG. I am a person. You will not know me. You do not know me.
        </div>
    </div>

    <script>
        const content = document.getElementById('mainContent');
        const hiddenMsg = document.getElementById('hiddenMsg');
        let isSelected = false;

        document.addEventListener('selectionchange', function() {
            const selection = window.getSelection();
            const selectedText = selection.toString();
            
            // Check if the selected text covers most of the content
            if (selectedText.length > 200) {
                if (!isSelected) {
                    isSelected = true;
                    content.style.display = 'none';
                    hiddenMsg.style.display = 'block';
                }
            } else {
                if (isSelected) {
                    isSelected = false;
                    content.style.display = 'block';
                    hiddenMsg.style.display = 'none';
                }
            }
        });

        // Also handle mouseup to catch selection
        document.addEventListener('mouseup', function() {
            const selection = window.getSelection();
            const selectedText = selection.toString();
            
            if (selectedText.length > 200) {
                if (!isSelected) {
                    isSelected = true;
                    content.style.display = 'none';
                    hiddenMsg.style.display = 'block';
                }
            } else {
                if (isSelected) {
                    isSelected = false;
                    content.style.display = 'block';
                    hiddenMsg.style.display = 'none';
                }
            }
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
